From aed470a1d0f565af1a591cb2e00875ee904a4c8d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shaun Adams <s.adams@f5.com>
Date: Sun, 14 Jun 2026 21:46:31 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 24/42] transports+configstore: PUT on
 /api/tenants/{tid}/providers/{provider}
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Closes the per-tenant admin surface for the three inference-plane
entities. Operators can now flip a tenant's provider concurrency,
network config, proxy, and OpenAI/custom provider fields without
recreating the row (which would invalidate the existing keys + any
VK provider configs that reference them). Keys carry over from the
existing row via an in-memory merge — rotation flows continue to use
the nested /keys routes from patch 0022.

configstore — UpdateProvider refactor:
- Extracted updateProviderInternal(ctx, tenantID, provider, config, tx)
  so the existing UpdateProvider and the new UpdateProviderForTenant
  share the key-cascade + VKPC-resync logic.
- updateProviderInternal scopes everything by tenant_id when non-empty:
  - Provider lookup gains WHERE tenant_id = ? so two tenants with
    same-named providers can't trample each other under the legacy
    or the new path.
  - VKPC lock acquisition now JOINs governance_virtual_keys and
    filters by virtual_keys.tenant_id, so we only lock the calling
    tenant's VKPCs (other tenants' rows stay available for concurrent
    UpdateVirtualKeyProviderConfig work).
  - Every newly created or save-updated TableKey pins tenant_id =
    tenantID so a future GetProviderKeys-by-tenant only returns the
    intended scope.
- UpdateProvider (legacy) is now a wrapper that calls
  updateProviderInternal with tenantID = tables.DefaultTenantID, so
  single-tenant deployments behave exactly as before but
  multi-tenant deployments using the legacy path can't accidentally
  reach into another tenant.
- UpdateProviderForTenant is the new public, tenant-explicit form.
- MockConfigStore stub added (single-implementation delegation).
- Tests cover: own-tenant update visible to GET; same-name providers
  in two tenants stay isolated under update; new keys added via the
  cascade get tenant_id pinned (defaultTenant GET should not see
  them); cross-tenant update returns ErrNotFound with the target
  row untouched.

Transport additions:
- handlers.TenantProviderHandler gains updateProvider under
  PUT /api/tenants/{tid}/providers/{provider}. Reuses the legacy
  providerUpdatePayload shape so the same UI / OpenAPI spec works
  for both the legacy /api/providers and the new tenant-scoped form.
  Reads the existing config to carry keys forward (the PUT body
  doesn't ship keys; rotation uses the nested /keys routes). Same
  validations as the legacy PUT (concurrency vs buffer, retry
  backoff, custom-provider immutability). On success: evicts the
  per-tenant runtime so the next inference acquires with the new
  concurrency / network config in scope.
- Handler tests cover: happy-path update with evict, missing parent
  404, invalid-concurrency-vs-buffer 400.

Ref: https://jira.f5net.com/browse/XC-25496
